  "what_this_is": "Directory entries as go-pmtiles decodes them, plus the raw compressed bytes they were decoded from. raster-z0z2 is the simple case with no repeats; dupes-z0z3 is the interesting one, with run_length > 1 and with several entries sharing an offset.",
  "how_each_number_was_obtained": {
    "raw_gzip_hex": "archive[root_offset : root_offset+root_length], read verbatim; this is the directory exactly as it sits in the file, still gzipped",
    "decompressed_hex": "the same bytes through compress/gzip in the dump program. This is a convenience, not a measurement: the entries below are the oracle.",
    "entries": "pmtiles.DeserializeEntries(bytes.NewBuffer(raw), header.InternalCompression); tile_id, offset, length and run_length are the EntryV3 fields verbatim",
    "z/x/y on each entry": "pmtiles.IDToZxy(tile_id), added so the entry is readable",
    "reserialize_roundtrip_ok": "pmtiles.SerializeEntries(entries, NoCompression) compared byte for byte against decompressed_hex. True means go-pmtiles' own serializer reproduces the directory body exactly, so a writer can be checked against decompressed_hex directly."
  },
  "invariants_worth_asserting": [
    "sum of run_length over all entries == header.addressed_tiles_count",
    "count of entries == header.tile_entries_count",
    "an entry with run_length == 0 is a leaf directory pointer, and its offset is relative to header.leaf_directory_offset, not to the start of the file",
    "entries are sorted by tile_id and the ids are strictly increasing",
    "a repeated offset means a deduplicated tile, and it does not have to be adjacent"
  ],
